The topic of the Gen Z star first came up on the Thursday (Oct. 22) episode of The New York Times&#8217; Popcast when hosts Jon Caramanica and Joe Coscarelli asked Corgan why he&#8217;s recently been championing younger artists such as YUNGBLUD and sombr. Rodrigo is an especially interesting case, they argued, because her songs — namely &#8220;The Cure&#8221; and &#8220;Pretty Isn&#8217;t Pretty,&#8221; which share a resemblance to &#8220;Disarm&#8221; and &#8220;1979,&#8221; respectively — have drawn comparisons to The Smashing Pumpkins&#8217; catalog.

But the Chicago band&#8217;s frontman implied that he finds the similarities flattering rather than objectionable. &#8220;She&#8217;s so smart,&#8221; Corgan raved of Rodrigo, whom he joined on stage for a duet of &#8220;33&#8221; at Lollapalooza this summer. &#8220;She&#8217;s super savvy.&#8221;

&#8220;I don&#8217;t know her much, but she&#8217;s figured out that the way to break free is to be free,&#8221; he continued. &#8220;She&#8217;s like, &#8216;Bring me all these influences.&#8217; She&#8217;s not afraid. She&#8217;s not afraid to make an imperfect song. She&#8217;s not afraid to have one vocal slightly out of tune &#8230; Pop stars should be as authentic in their game as rock stars are authentic in their game.&#8221;

Corgan also agreed that it&#8217;s been freeing connecting with younger artists, because they weren&#8217;t around when The Smashing Pumpkins received poor reviews on albums that are now heralded as classics, meaning their opinions of him are shaped purely by music.

He&#8217;s hardly the first rock star to sing Rodrigo&#8217;s praises. Crow has lauded her multiple times, calling her the &#8220;real deal&#8221; on The Tonight Show in 2023, and Jagger told Billboard in the Rolling Stones&#8217; cover story earlier this year, &#8220;She’s really good at [rock music] &#8230; the ability to change styles from what you think [her] original girly pop stuff is — it’s kind of interesting.&#8221;

Morrissette and Nicks joined Rodrigo at her inaugural Daisy Chain Fields festival, and White has kept in contact with the former Disney star since they met — and he called her &#8220;very cool, very real&#8221; — in 2022. Smith partnered up with Rodrigo for a rare collaboration on &#8220;What&#8217;s Wrong With Me,&#8221; which is featured on her Billboard 200 -topping third studio album, you seem pretty sad for a girl so in love.

“Olivia’s desire to be recognized as a songwriter is very refreshing,&#8221; The Cure frontman told The Hollywood Reporter earlier in October. &#8220;It’s unmodern in a way &#8230; She was in London with me a while back. She played me something she wrote that morning, things that could take 14 years for many writers to get out, and she does it in a morning.”

